592186281134 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186281134 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186280365 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186281134 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "aec5203e-7431-5285-804f-2b85f96ff86c" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186281267 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186278638 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186281267 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186278897 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186281267 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186279488 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186281267 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186279785 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186281267 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186279929 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186281267 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186281267 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186281267 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186279929 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186281267 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "f48d194b-9d36-54e9-be97-ae912aef2d30" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186281284 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186281267 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186281284 #edb/ref 1069 "q-161652" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186281284 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186281284 #edb/ref 1071 "Consider the set $A,$ defined by \n\n$$\nA=\\{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,1<{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}<4\\}.\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?  \n\nI. $∂A\\cap A\\ne ∅$\n\nII. $\\text{int}\\,A\\cap ∂A=∅$\n\nIII. $A=\\text{int}\\,A$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186281284 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "46773dfb-2950-5619-a7ba-c3559b8d83bf" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186281284 #edb/ref 1074 "The boundary of a set $A,$ denoted $∂A,$ is the set that contains all the boundary points of $A.$\n\nIn this case, the set $A$ and its boundary $∂A={C}_{1}\\cup {C}_{2}$ are shown below.\n\n![](images/22/2273cd843c4bfaeaff10d49d3400d7661262673639a66034638d805eef5b1e47.png)\n\n   \n\nThe interior of a set $A,$ denoted $\\text{int}\\,A,$ is the set containing all the interior points of $A.$ It contains every point in $A$ except the boundary points: \n\n$$\n\\text{int}\\,A=A-∂A\n$$\n\nThe interior of $A$ is shown below.\n\n![](images/5e/5e473584ef5193b434ff6c138b08c4fbd9111a37252019143b1afb2d48c913c6.png)\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each statement:\n\n- Statement I is false. As we've seen, $A$ contains none of its boundary points, so we must have  $∂A\\cap A=∅.$\n\n- Statement II is true. Since $\\text{int}\\,A$ contains all points in $A$ except the boundary points, we must have $\\text{int}\\,A\\cap ∂A=∅,$ where $∅$ denotes the empty set.\n\n- Statement III is true. Since $A$ contains none of its boundary points, we must have $A=\\text{int}\\,A.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III  only.\"" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186281303 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186281134 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186281303 #edb/ref 1069 "q-161702" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186281303 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186281303 #edb/ref 1071 "![](images/84/84806884f843154c17c338eef0f50d83cae049aece675450e21e58dade6a9f34.png)\n\nConsider the set $A$ shown above. The interior of $A$ is \n\n$$\n\\text{int}\\,A=\\{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,\\bbox[5px,border: 1px solid black]{\\phantom{AAAA}}\\}.\n$$\n\nWhat is the missing expression?" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186281303 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "45bc0b9a-3391-5849-aa6e-c42fba251f8a" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186281303 #edb/ref 1074 "The boundary of a set $A,$ denoted $∂A,$ is the set that contains all the boundary points of $A.$\n\nThe set $A$ and its boundary $∂A$ are shown below.\n\n![](images/ce/ce268d8b396ea63227734c1edd6b876bb0fe9755fa12a3b75be90c6ef4af5af3.png)\n\nThe interior of a set $A,$ denoted $\\text{int}\\,A,$ is the set containing all the interior points of $A.$ It contains every point in $A$ except the boundary points: \n\n$$\n\\text{int}\\,A=A-∂A\n$$\n\nThe interior of $A$ is shown below.\n\n![](images/84/84780a84406a3fd0e281737b979887e0de6b1e9fe39d440f379fbb2b84e80a3b.png)\n\nSo, in this case, the interior of $A$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\text{int}\\,A=\\{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,{x}^{2}-1<y<0\\}.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186407100 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186407108 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186407100 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186407109 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186407100 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186407110 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186407100 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186407111 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186407100 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186407112 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186407100 #edb/ref 1044 #edb/ref 17592186045464 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186407100 #edb/ref 1045 "Interiors and Boundaries of Sets" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186407100 #edb/ref 1046 #edb/ref 17592186407109 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186407100 #edb/ref 1048 #edb/ref 17592186046659 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186407100 #edb/ref 1049 #edb/ref 17592186048621 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186407100 #edb/ref 1053 #uuid "76e2698b-8be0-5d8e-90fa-0fb9464d3b79" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186407101 #edb/ref 1080 "0<x<2" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186407101 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186407101 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "1343a63e-0338-5507-8d29-781c61de7f44" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186407102 #edb/ref 1080 "-2<x<2" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186407102 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186407102 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "24a9296e-4eb0-5d98-9be7-848968667f9d" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186407103 #edb/ref 1080 "-2<x<0" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186407103 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186407103 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "75e8591a-dc02-55dc-ad14-ef68af4fe858" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186407104 #edb/ref 1080 "-2\\le x\\le 0" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186407104 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186407104 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid 